# Cursor Rules — Forge Project

## Project context

Go 1.24+, module `github.com/teragrid/forge`, CGO_ENABLED=0.
Single binary CLI. Cobra framework. One package per verb under `internal/cli/cmd<verb>/`.

## Code style

- Standard Go formatting (`gofmt`). No goimports aliases.
- Table-driven tests. No third-party test frameworks.
- Error wrapping: `fmt.Errorf("context: %w", err)`.
- Use `errcode.New` / `errcode.Newf` for user-facing errors.
- Comments on exported symbols only.

## Key constraints

- No `os.Exit` outside `cmd/forge/main.go`
- No CGO
- No new third-party dependencies without an ADR
- All LLM calls via `internal/llmprovider`
- All subprocesses via `internal/procspawn`
- All file path access validated via `internal/fssandbox`

## Adding a verb

1. Create `internal/cli/cmd<verb>/<verb>.go` with `New() *cobra.Command`
2. Add `verbmeta.Register(...)` in `init()`
3. Register error codes (see `docs/ERROR_CODES.md`)
4. Add to `internal/cli/root.go`

## Before committing

```
go build ./...
go vet ./...
go test ./...
```

All three must produce zero errors/failures.

## Error code ranges (quick ref)

- 1000–1999: core verbs (init, new, add, doctor)
- 2000–2999: scan family
- 3000–3999: fix / review / explain
- 4000–4999: LLM / plugin infrastructure
- 5000–5999: ship / deploy / agents / report
- 6000–6999: reserved for future use

See `docs/ERROR_CODES.md` for the full registry.
